+// CacheBypassedKvGatedPrefixDecider extends CacheAwareKvGatedPrefixDecider with a
+// per-request "cache-magnitude switch": when the request's cached-prefix size on the
+// selected decode pod is >= cacheCapTokens, the transient-KV gate is bypassed entirely
+// and the decision reduces to QD-only (LoadGatedPrefix behavior). When cachedTokens <
+// cacheCapTokens, the full OR-combined (QD ∨ transientKvUtil) gate from
+// CacheAwareKvGatedPrefixDecider is evaluated.
+//
+// Formula:
+//
+//	nonCachedTokens = len(req.InputTokens) − cachedBlocks × blockSize
+//	cachedTokens    = cachedBlocks × blockSize
+//	qdFires         = (selected.QueueDepth >= queueGate)
+//	kvFires         = false
+//	if cachedTokens < cacheCapTokens:
+//	    transientKvTokens = max(0, KvTokensInUse − cachedTokens)
+//	    transientKvUtil   = transientKvTokens / TotalKvCapacityTokens  (0 if capacity ≤ 0)
